Module skeel "Fair Weather" {
  Description "What a ranger can read in the Pulpit that nobody else would look at: the print of a boot in the red clay, and whose boot it was. A second way to the same truth as the boy's, by the ground and not the sea.".

  // ── The ranger's way ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The boy on Seal Skerry saw what the Reeve did on the Strand. The ground in the Pulpit saw what he did before it:
  // the hook, the lantern, and the man who stood there a long time, and then ran. Anyone can see the hook (it is on the
  // Pulpit's list of things to look at). Only someone who reads ground sees the man.
  Discovery boot_prints "In the lee of the Pulpit's back wall, in a skin of red clay that the wind cannot reach, the print of a left boot, iron-heeled, with the third nail of the heel missing: a tall man, standing a long time, and then going down the edge faster than he came up.".
  Action read_pulpit_ground(actor: group, site: place, r: member) "Read the clay in the lee of the Pulpit's back wall" {
    Description "Everything else up here has been scoured by the wind. There is one place it does not reach.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, pulpit) and memberOf(r, actor)
      and hasCalling(r, calling_ranger) and awake(r) and knows(actor, hook_found) and not knows(actor, boot_prints).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, boot_prints). }
    Result "{r} goes down on hands and knees in the niche, with the wind shouting overhead, and puts a cheek almost to the rock. In the angle of the back wall the clay is red and damp and has kept something. 'There,' {r} says. 'One man, tall, left foot a shade turned in. He stood here from before the moon was up till the ship struck. Look how deep the toes are: he was leaning on the hook.' A finger hovers over the heel. 'Iron on the heel, and the third nail gone, so the print has a bite out of it.' Then, lower: 'And the next prints are twice as far apart.'".
  }
  Observe boots_by_the_stove at reeve_parlour when knows(party, boot_prints) "A pair of big black boots stands by the parlour stove, drying, the left one worn down on its outer edge. The iron on the left heel is short of a nail; the third one is gone, and has left a bite. Red clay is dried in the welt, the red that is only on the Craigs path." teaches boots_match.
  Discovery boots_match "The Reeve's left boot has its third heel-nail missing, and Craigs clay in the welt: the same boot that stood in the Pulpit.".
  Rule put_together_boots when knows(party, hook_found) and knows(party, boot_prints) and knows(party, boots_match) and not knows(party, hender_did)
    says "A hook driven new into a crack, and a boot-print with a bite out of the heel, and the same bite in a boot that dries by a stove in Fore Street. You did not need a boy on a hatch to tell you whose. You need only to know that he stood there a long time first." teaches hender_did { }
}
